  "term": "residence rate",
  "definition": "In this historical asylum-statistics usage, residence rate means the length or average duration of patients’ stay in an institution. It refers to studying how long residents remain, often by comparing the periods of residence across groups such as those who recovered, improved, died, or were still in the asylum.",
